WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.070
Please wait, Ryo-sama!

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.740
So damn persistent!

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.040
Enough is enough!

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.590
You idiot!

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.210
If you go on, I’ll kick you out!

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.540
You jinx!

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.670
Ryo-sama! That’s cruel!

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.170
So so cruel!

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:32.170
I’ve been asking you
to call me by my name.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.180
Oh, that?!

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.180
Damn, she doesn’t know how to give up.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.950
Why is this happening to me?

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.620
It’s so tough for you.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.910
You don’t know how the girl feels.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.700
The more you run away, the more she’ll want to chase after you.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.130
Don’t analyze it so calmly.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:03.470
Just think of me, suffering from a proposal by a complete stranger.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.470
I think I know the feeling myself.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:07.550
Oh yeah?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.050
Yeah. I have a total stranger as my fiancé too.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:27.490
So I don’t spill my wish from my eyes,

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:34.350
I want to make my heart race to you.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:41.710
I put my feelings on this palette of endearment

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:47.340
and paint them on my heart.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.260
The sweetness

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.230
is drawing bells in the sky.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:11.360
Colorful assortments of balloons of dreams

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.250
float in the wind,

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.130
flowing toward you,

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:18.600
freely.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:25.420
I’m happy that I found destiny.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.050
It’s filling with colors.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:34.050
The Departure to
Love and Ambition?!
A Great Decision!

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.520
One day, my parents handed me a photo and told me,

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.550
“This is your fiancé.”

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.560
He’s the heir to a company that my father’s business deals with.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.650
Hey, that’s…

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.360
Yup, it’s a political marriage.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.490
Th-That’s not right!

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.210
You’ve never met him, right?

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.200
No.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.450
And they’re making you marry him?

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.410
I guess so.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:01.000
You guess so?

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.450
Emi-rin, are you okay with that?

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.960
It doesn’t matter,
I don’t have the authority to decide.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.260
N-No way…

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.890
Ojo, don’t mind them.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.420
Turn that marriage proposal down!

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.770
We’ll help you as much as you want!

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.100
Yeah, yeah!

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.430
If they’re still persistent, then leave your home!

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.690
As a last resort, take a stand!

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.990
It’s not a laughing matter.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.490
He’s right, Emi-rin!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.280
Sorry.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.620
I was just happy that I have two friends who get so seriously concerned about me.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.540
But I’m not complaining about this situation.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.630
As long as I tell myself that this is normal…

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.690
Or at least, I’d been convinced it was normal ever since I was a child.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:52.500
Emiho… Emiho!

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.580
Coming!

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.380
When you get older,
you’ll be the greatest bride in all of Japan.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.410
And I’ll find the greatest groom to match you.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.400
Okay!

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.250
It looks so good on you, Ojo-sama!

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.920
You might wind up
overshadowing the bride.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.290
Emiho-sama will look even better
when she gets married, won’t she?

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:18.610
Oh my, Emiho caught the bouquet?

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.910
There’s no doubt in my mind that Emiho will be

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.060
an even more gorgeous bride than the one we saw today.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.460
Oh, you…

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.910
Well, it’s a bit early, but it’s just like an arranged date.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.010
But they didn’t give you any choice!

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.920
What’s most important is the will of the marrying parties themselves!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.840
To accept the marriage arrangement my parents recommended,

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.760
can’t that also be my will?

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.660
That’s not the point!

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.010
I’m saying that it’s wrong for them to decide on your marriage

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.560
without your knowledge about it!

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.250
Mizuhara…

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.560
Why are you being so adamant about my issue?

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.170
Why? Well…

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.570
My space got invaded by a stupid stranger, and…

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:04.430
In your case, it’s not that you don’t know her, but that you’re trying to avoid knowing her.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:08.560
You’re so upset about
the Department of RTP,

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.920
that you can’t see who she really is.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.400
You’re trying not to see her.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.360
W-Well…

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:18.950
You’ve been living alone with your little sister since you both were young,

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:22.370
and you had to decide
everything on your own.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.870
And that made you refuse forceful decisions cast upon you

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.960
by higher powers such as parents and teachers.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.100
Isn’t that right?

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.150
H-Hey, but this and that are not…

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:35.970
They are the same.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:42.530
After all, you just can’t stand me obeying my parents so blindly.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:44.740
Mizuhara,

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:50.060
I want to spend more energy on befriending the person I’m bound to be together with

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:55.110
rather than searching for the special someone I don’t know if I’ll be able to meet.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.460
I don’t think I’m wrong about it.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:58.840
So…

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.760
let’s not talk about it anymore.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.990
See ya, Ryo, Emi-rin.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.110
Yeah, see ya.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:15.880
Oh yes.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:20.280
It’s a good chance – I have
something else I want to tell you.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.390
No matter what the reason,
you’re now living together.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:28.160
At least call her by her name.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.530
Her?

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.020
Oh, that idiot.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.390
Ryo-sama!
Oh, that idiot.

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:33.190
Mizuhara,

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:40.000
if my partner kept calling me an idiot and nasty…

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.160
Calm down a little.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.700
Even between you and her,
had you met differently,

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.830
nobody knows how your relationship might have been.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:53.460
Well, it may be none of my business.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:04.550
I’m home.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.300
Yay!

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.020
I caught you!

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.360
H-Hey!

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:17.520
Even if you keep running away from me at school, you have to come home.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.730
Of course.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.170
Anyway, get off of me.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.900
Before that, the welcome home…

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.990
I told you to get off!

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.600
Geez! Ryo-sama, you’re so cold!

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:31.580
Sheesh.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.350
Don’t tell me you were waiting for this all night.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:40.210
Oh, you were studying?

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.300
Wait, do we have any homework?

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:45.050
No, I’m just studying for myself.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:50.060
Then before you start clinging to me,
take your classes more seriously.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:55.310
Yeah, but 11th grade classes are completely beyond me,

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:58.460
so I’m studying the material for 10th grade classes, where I belong anyway.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:03.650
Oh, dinner is ready, so I’ll go get it.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.280
Oh? Was it your turn tonight?

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.300
No. Akane-san told me that she was going to be late because of her club activities.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.580
But she should be home soon.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.130
Ryo-sama, go ahead
and change your clothes.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:19.810
Yeah…

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.520
She…

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:29.780
even vacuumed and did laundry.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:35.270
You are so upset about the Department of RTP

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:37.540
that you can’t see who she really is.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.230
I see…

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:46.110
She was stretching just so that she could be with me.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.030
That idiot.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.700
Really?

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:52.590
Really!

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.790
It’s hard to believe!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.140
Ryo-sama, would you like seconds?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:02.830
No…

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:05.940
Did you not like the dinner?

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.130
Oh, it was delicious.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:09.950
Thank you.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:12.050
Good!

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.830
Then I would like to have a prize.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.650
A prize?!

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.280
Yes!

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:22.710
Would you please call me Shizuka?

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:26.460
You’re still thinking about that?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.090
I can’t have it?

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.360
Ryo-sama…

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.470
Please! Please!?

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.920
It was good.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.560
Thanks, Shizuka.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.210
Brother…

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.570
That’s what you wanted, right?

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.050
Yes!

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.960
If we had met differently, huh?

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:10.130
But, the reality is,
we can’t change our encounter.

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:15.800
As long as that reality exists,
my feelings won’t change either.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.330
But it’s different for Ojo.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:27.000
To accept the marriage arrangement my parents recommended,

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.060
can’t that also be my will?

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.130
In your case,

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.570
it’s not that you don’t know her, but that you’re trying to avoid knowing her.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:35.510
Sheesh.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:39.070
She’s trying to avoid knowing me too.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:43.650
That’s right!

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:46.860
And they’re trying to decide for people they’ve never met?!

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:54.010
I’m not convinced!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.130
Ojo, come with me.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:04.920
How are you going to talk me out of it this time?

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:08.350
There’s no talking you out of it.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:12.590
I’m just veeeeery bad at giving up.

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:15.390
I’m not trying to brag,
but I’m stubborn too.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:15.950
Yeah.

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:20.020
So I won’t tell you anything

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:22.870
as long as you choose the partner your parents chose, on your own will.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:24.720
I see.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:25.960
In that case…

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:26.440
But…

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:32.880
before that!

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:38.760
Ojo,

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.850
go on a date with me.

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:53.220
Wait, Brother, what’s this?!

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:55.200
Are you sure about this?!

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:57.360
After shocking little sister he lived with for 15 years,

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.360
it’s going to continue in the next episode!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.780
To be continued

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:05.730
The moment came

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.730
very much out of the blue.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:14.870
You showed up right in front of me,

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:17.590
then started to change everything.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.420
If my meeting you

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.270
is not by fate,

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:30.630
there are no miracles,

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:35.820
even if I search all over the world.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:39.210
Embracing love,

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:43.140
kissing love,

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:47.070
holding love,

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:51.370
I whisper, “I love you.”

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.400
Please look at me and me alone,

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.820
forever.
